 ASYST Strengthens Global Partnerships at DVN Shanghai 2026


 ASYST Technologies was proud to exhibit at the DVN Shanghai Lighting Workshop, held September 8-9, 2026, in Shanghai, China. Bringing together more than 500 automotive lighting professionals from around the world, the event provided an excellent opportunity to connect with OEMs, Tier 1 suppliers, engineers, designers, and industry leaders shaping the future of vehicle lighting.
At our booth, ASYST showcased our core automotive lighting solutions, including motor carriers, ball sockets, aiming adjusters, heat sinks, and other critical headlamp components. With more than 30 years of experience supporting the automotive industry, we were pleased to discuss how our precision-engineered products help manufacturers deliver reliable, high-performance lighting systems.
This year’s workshop focused on the theme, “Vehicle Lighting Experience: Technology, Innovation, Safety and Design,” featuring discussions on emerging technologies such as advanced projection systems, MicroLEDs, ADAS integration, AI-driven lighting development tools, and next-generation vehicle lighting architectures.
For ASYST, the event was a valuable opportunity to strengthen existing relationships, develop new partnerships, and gain insight into the latest trends driving innovation across the global automotive lighting market.
Thank you to everyone who visited our booth and connected with our team. We look forward to building on these relationships, expanding our presence in China, and continuing to support the future of automotive lighting worldwide.
Sales team at Shanghai DVN

















